# Pre-code source and history record

The project skill/workflow, current stream/batch state and problem anchor,
research-lit and proof-writer instructions were read. Tool discovery had no
Zotero/Obsidian capability; the arXiv helper was absent, so direct arXiv/web
metadata and primary pages were used. Local paper filenames were checked
first, with original TeX selected for exact internal rules. No secondary
website is used as authority for a technical theorem.

## Primary body actually inspected

Asinowski, Banderier and Hackl, *Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of
pop-stack sorting*, DMTCS 22:2 (2021), article 4. Primary publisher PDF:
https://dmtcs.episciences.org/7411/pdf ; author metadata:
https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.04912 . The actual PDF text for section 1.1 and
section 2.1/Theorem 3 with proof was read through the browser (39-page PDF;
browser text lines 39--125 and 663--689). Full-paper reading is not claimed.
The paper reverses every maximal decreasing run, not selected odd runs.
Complementing values identifies its operator with reversal of every
increasing run. ORR's parity selection is not that identical literal: for
$12$ ORR holds, while the complemented all-run rule gives $21$.
This difference is not a novelty certificate. Ordinary run reversal,
inversion potential and run-partition inverse language are deducted.

